course: dictionary
lesson: 12169
title: Comprise: what makes up a whole
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Comprise is a formal word, often found in reports and exams. It tells you what something is made of, or what parts make up a whole. «The class comprises 15 boys and 12 girls.» The class is made of those children, so you can count them: 27 children in the class.
explain: You can also say a thing is comprised of its parts. «The kit is comprised of a hammer, a saw and some nails.» Both «comprises» and «is comprised of» tell you the parts that build the whole. The whole comes first, and the parts come after.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler phrase. Try «consists of» or «is made up of» in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have understood comprise. «The team comprises five players» means «The team is made up of five players.»
fact: Comprise means to be made up of certain parts, or to consist of them.
fact: «The class comprises 15 boys and 12 girls» means the class is made of those children, so there are 27 children.
fact: Comprise can also mean to make up or form a whole, but some people think this use is wrong.
fact: Forms of the word: comprise, comprises, comprised, comprising.
fact: Some people think «comprise of» is wrong, so use «comprise» or «be comprised of» to be safe.
exercise: «The class comprises 15 boys and 12 girls.» How many children are in the class? | 12 | *27 | 3 | 15
exercise: «The team comprises five players.» What does comprises mean? | *Is made up of | Cancels | Runs away from | Wins against
exercise: «The box comprises six small cakes.» Which phrase could replace comprises? | jumps over | *consists of | runs from | tastes like
test: Which sentence uses comprise to show the parts that make up a whole? | The pizza is loudly singing | *The pizza comprises cheese, tomato and dough | The pizza is very green | The pizza runs fast
test: «The garden is comprised of lawn and trees.» What does comprised mean here? | *made up of | painted over | sold to | grew from
exam: «The school comprises three buildings.» How many buildings make up the school? | 1 | 2 | *3 | 4
